WEBVTT

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.980
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.820
You really are pathetic.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.530
What?!

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:38.290
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.210
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:45.050
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:14.220
<i>The train is approaching at Platform 13.</i>

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:17.940
<i>Please stand behind the yellow line.</i>

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.810
<i>Today was really funny, huh?</i>

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.770
<i>You think she's still
looking for her shoes?</i>

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.860
<i>Seeing her look through the trash
was funny.</i>

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:31.030
<i>And when she still couldn't find them
and started crying. Hilarious!</i>

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:36.870
<i>So, how should we play with her tomorrow?</i>

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.110
Watch it!

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:50.900
I can't believe he didn't even apologize.
I'm gonna burn him on the internet!

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:06.860
What...?

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:09.510
What is this...?

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:10.530
CHAPTER 7

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:15.510
GHOST TRAIN

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.770
<i>Yokai</i>? Ghosts?

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:24.590
Believing in that stuff is proof
of one's idiocy!

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:27.250
Huh. You think so?

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:32.050
I've had it with all the idiots recently!

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.020
Come to think of it, who was that guy?

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.890
The one who quit recently.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.690
Uh... You mean Sugimoto-san?

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:43.230
Or... Shiota <i>senpai</i>?!

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:46.590
Yeah, that's it! That Shio guy, Shio!

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:57.850
He said,
"Maybe you can't see them, but I can."

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:01.290
Going on about
nonexistent ghosts and <i>yokai</i>.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.770
Talk about a hopeless case.

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:04.960
Huh...

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.090
If I may interject.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:13.030
Even if you can't see it,
what's there is there.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:14.320
What?!

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.930
Let's not, Kitaro. Getting involved
with a guy like this is a waste of time.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:20.810
A guy like this?!

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.900
Listen, you bums.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.690
I'm a company president!

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:31.820
My company may be small,
but I still feed 30 employees!

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:36.870
Ooh! Well, well.
I thought you seemed well-refined.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:42.600
Well then, Mr. President, would you be
willing to buy the poor bums a drink?

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:44.920
Hah? Idiot!

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.920
People have to earn what they eat
for themselves!

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:53.300
Failures like you who can't do that
don't deserve to live!

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.610
Wait, Mr. President!

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:59.100
Talking about what can't be seen!
<i>Yokai</i> and ghosts!

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:04.230
People who make up excuses are
nothing more than trash! Worthless trash!

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:06.830
You really are pathetic.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:08.580
What?!

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.570
H-Hey, Kitaro!

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:16.590
That suits you, you piece of trash!

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:21.250
Have you ever heard of karmatic justice?

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.410
Huh?

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.370
Remember...

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:30.940
What goes around comes around.

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:40.120
Come on, let's go!

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:41.760
Wait for me!

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:43.720
I'm sorry.

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:47.440
They've gone.

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:52.690
I heard about this, but it really is ugly.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:05:59.660
Dammit all!

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:04.100
Thanks to those weirdos,
we've missed the last train.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:04.040
NOTICE - SPECIAL TRAIN

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.330
No, I think we're still good.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:07.380
What?

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.690
Look.

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:12.150
12:42 AM for Tama Cemetery?

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:14.130
Was there always such a train?

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:16.510
Oh, excuse me, sir!

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:22.430
That's not a mistake, right?

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:25.910
Yes. It's a special train just for today.

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:28.890
Thank goodness! Let's hurry.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:30.610
But...

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:33.170
Mr. President, aren't you always saying,

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:36.300
"Making swift decisions is
the key to victory"?

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.800
You're a hundred years too young
to say that.

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:55.260
Say, is it always this quiet
for the last train?

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:58.240
Everyone's probably just tired.

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:00.780
You think?

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:07.690
It looks like the train's coming.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.500
I can see that.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:18.860
It's like the doors to a crematory...

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.370
Don't say ominous stuff like that.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.240
Mr. President, hurry!

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:44.680
There's a seat over here.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:45.970
Right.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:51.370
All aboard.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:38.380
I don't know about this, but if we can
go home by train, I'm satisfied.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:41.950
Yes. I can finally go home, too.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:45.510
What? You haven't been home recently?

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:48.040
No. Not for about two weeks...

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:52.540
Honestly. That's because
you're always such a slow worker.

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:58.130
But meeting quotas is absolute, even if it
means staying over or working all night.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:00.630
Doing so much goes without saying.

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:01.730
Well...

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:14.250
Everyone's really gloomy.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:19.290
It's like we're at a wake.

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:24.360
Don't be so morbid.

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:31.660
What's wrong?

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:34.710
N-Nothing...

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:45.610
What is this...?

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:49.950
Huh?

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:51.950
I'm sorry.

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:58.040
A ringtone? Talk about poor taste.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:02.360
Turn off the sound on the train! Honestly!

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:10.870
Ticket inspection.

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:14.260
Inspection? In this day and age?

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:22.770
Your tickets, please.

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:30.050
Here.

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:34.730
Sir, this pass expired a week ago.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:38.000
What? That's impossible!

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.500
He's right. But don't worry.

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:44.860
I made sure to buy two tickets.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:46.570
Don't you have a pass?

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:51.510
A pass isn't worth it
if I'm not going home for a week.

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:55.120
But, a ticket?

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:57.450
I like how it has a bit of charm.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.880
-Here.
-R-Right.

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:01.420
Thanks.

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:04.130
TO TAMA CEMETERY

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:04.190
Six <i>mon</i>?

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:09.860
260 yen...

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:15.310
Next is Crematory. Crematory.

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:18.440
Crematory? Was there a station like that?

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:22.480
That's strange. I'll go ask.

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:30.950
A river...?

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:33.390
We never cross a river like this...

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:42.230
H-Hey! That...

00:11:49.460 --> 00:11:50.550
Hey!

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:14.130
STATIONMASTER KITARO

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:18.640
GHOST TRAIN

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:17.580
<i>-"Yeah, yeah. You're hot and cold."
-"Huh?!"</i>

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:18.580
<i>"What'd I do?"</i>

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:21.770
Mr. President, wake up.

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:24.000
I was...

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.960
Are you all right? You fell over.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:29.010
Th-That's right...

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:30.210
I...

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:33.760
Dammit!

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:36.510
<i>What was that?</i>

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:39.640
<i>A dream? It felt rather...</i>

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:42.000
What?

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:49.740
Are you all right?

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:54.050
If it still hurts tomorrow,
maybe you should go to a hospital.

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:56.080
I know a good place.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:59.710
It's where Kunishige <i>senpai</i> stayed
when he got sick.

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:01.210
Kunishige?

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:04.000
Oh yeah, there was an employee like that.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.960
But, I haven't seen him recently.

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:09.000
Of course not.

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:16.160
Right after he was discharged,
he killed himself by jumping into a river.

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:21.970
His body may have healed,
but not his heart...

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:26.150
What an idiot! A born loser if you ask me.

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:29.880
He was incompetent, so that's why
he got depressed and died in the end.

00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:33.210
Is that so...?

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:44.810
Hey, what's with that look?

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:52.420
Mr. President...

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:09.750
Kunishige...?

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:13.530
O-Oh, you're alive!

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:16.840
Honestly. You and your dumb lies.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:19.200
Look, Kunishige's...

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:23.370
But...

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:28.620
I-It's wet!

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:33.550
Shiota...?

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:35.690
Sugimoto...?!

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:40.050
Shibazaki...!

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:47.290
What's wrong?

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:50.770
You look like you've seen a ghost.

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:53.650
Th-That's not true.

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:57.300
B-Besides, ghosts don't exist.

00:14:57.300 --> 00:14:58.880
You're right.

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:03.000
<i>That's right. Ghosts don't exist.</i>

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:06.250
<i>I haven't done anything to
deserve being haunted...</i>

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:10.090
People like you never take initiative!

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:11.690
Use your head!

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:15.470
-I heard about you from your last job!
-I'm sorry!

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:18.970
-You were useless so you got laid off!
-I'm sorry!

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:21.390
You've got nowhere else to go!

00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:24.310
What goes around comes around!

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:29.390
If you're going to quit, then pay me back
for what it's cost to train you!

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:33.170
Listen, these are lashings of love!

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:38.280
I'm saying this because I care about you!

00:15:38.650 --> 00:15:42.260
I... understand...

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:48.170
What's wrong?

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:49.430
N-Nothing...

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:52.880
<i>It's fine. I'm not wrong.</i>

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:55.400
<i>That's what a job is.</i>

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:59.150
That's right. That's why...

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:02.010
it wasn't my fault.

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:16.770
Th-That was...

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:20.300
The one who jumped and killed himself...

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:23.280
Ah, at last...

00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:27.200
You finally remember...

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:39.500
Mr. President...

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.640
Please open up!

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:57.900
Open up! Please open up!

00:16:58.610 --> 00:17:00.840
-What's wrong?
-M-Monsters!

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:02.800
Monsters?

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:05.700
By monsters,

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:08.870
do you mean things like these?

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:23.280
I'm getting off this train!

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:25.680
Even if I have to force my way off it!

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:52.970
What is this...?

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:54.520
What's going on...?

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:03.590
You can't get off this train.

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:04.610
You...!

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:08.200
What is all of this? What's happening?!

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:11.200
This is a train to Hell.

00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:12.660
Hell?!

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:17.230
When you were alive,
you earned the malice of many people.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:19.560
You bullied and drove them to death.

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:22.280
You're going to get what's coming.

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:24.200
When I was alive?!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:25.210
Yes.

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:29.990
What are you talking about?!
I'm perfectly fine!

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:33.290
I've got both my feet! I'm not a ghost...

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.390
See?

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:41.550
You're already dead.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.510
You were hit by a train.

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:47.300
But you just refused to admit it.

00:18:47.650 --> 00:18:49.430
That's...

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:50.890
I was...

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:53.620
hit by a train?

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:04.980
It's not true. That was...

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:07.110
It is true.

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:09.280
That was a week ago.

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:12.120
But, it was so sudden.

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:15.310
You didn't realize your own death.

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:20.310
Normally, you should have
gotten straight on this train.

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:23.050
But, you wandered as a ghost.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:27.220
Every night, you made some excuse
to miss the last train,

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:30.340
and avoided going to the afterlife.

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:37.620
That's why the people waiting in
the afterlife who bear malice towards you

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:41.440
got tired of waiting and came for you.

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:47.300
Saying, "Hurry to the afterlife."

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:51.160
-You can't escape.
-We've been waiting for you.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:53.790
And, "Go to Hell."

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.620
Let's go.

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:05.090
URN
NEXT STOP HELL / PREVIOUS STOP CREMATORY

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:05.150
Urn. Urn.

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:10.670
The next station is the final stop, Hell.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:15.660
N-No! I don't want to go to Hell!

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:17.030
Help me!

00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:22.270
Have you ever helped anyone
who said that to you?

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:24.230
Please!

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:27.800
Hey! How can you call yourself human?!

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:30.760
I'm not a human.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:46.290
No!!

00:20:54.740 --> 00:20:58.200
So, what I saw a week ago was...

00:20:58.470 --> 00:21:04.360
Yes. He died, consumed by
the substantial malice of others.

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:07.980
Last night,
he finally passed on to the afterlife.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:14.070
You said you were too scared
to go to that station.

00:21:14.070 --> 00:21:18.010
Those hands
existed only to push that man off.

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:23.620
So, you don't have to worry about
getting pushed off by those hands.

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:26.350
You can erase that photo, too.

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:28.210
I see...

00:21:30.190 --> 00:21:31.530
ERASE IMAGE?
NO / YES

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:37.700
Yes. Unless you can think of a reason
that they might.

00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:39.950
<i>What do we do today?</i>

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:41.490
<i>What'll we play?</i>

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:46.820
This was a human
bullying other humans to their deaths

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:50.480
and that malice went on
to kill another human.

00:21:50.820 --> 00:21:52.500
That's all it is.

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:55.510
<i>You think she'll still fight back?</i>

00:21:55.510 --> 00:21:58.370
<i>I wish she'd just disappear.</i>

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:03.020
It's far more frightening than a <i>yokai</i>.

00:22:06.250 --> 00:22:07.420
<i>oeoeo</i>

00:22:06.250 --> 00:22:07.420
<i>Oeoeo</i>

00:22:07.540 --> 00:22:08.790
<i>oeoeo</i>

00:22:07.540 --> 00:22:08.790
<i>Oeoeo</i>

00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:11.460
<i>oeoeoeoeo</i>

00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:11.460
<i>Oeoeoeoeo</i>

00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:16.470
<i>mienaimono ni koso shinjitsu ga
arukamo nante</i>

00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:16.470
<i>Perhaps the truth lies
In what you can't see</i>

00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:19.340
<i>kimi wa shinjirukana? me wo tojireba</i>

00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:19.340
<i>Do you believe that?
If you close your eyes</i>

00:22:19.470 --> 00:22:23.930
<i>hajimaruyo atarashii monogatari</i>

00:22:19.470 --> 00:22:23.930
<i>A new story will begin</i>

00:22:24.890 --> 00:22:30.190
<i>taisetsu na mono wa itsudatte</i>

00:22:24.890 --> 00:22:30.190
<i>The really important things</i>

00:22:30.310 --> 00:22:34.990
<i>me niwa mienai monosa</i>

00:22:30.310 --> 00:22:34.990
<i>Are always things you can't see</i>

00:22:35.110 --> 00:22:37.820
<i>namae no nai sora wo miage</i>

00:22:35.110 --> 00:22:37.820
<i>Looking up to a nameless sky</i>

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:40.950
<i>hiki komogomo yume wo kazoeta</i>

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:40.950
<i>I bittersweetly counted dreams</i>

00:22:41.070 --> 00:22:43.580
<i>kimi wa jibun ni shoujikikai?</i>

00:22:41.070 --> 00:22:43.580
<i>Are you honest with yourself?</i>

00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:48.500
<i>kaze ga hana wo kusugutta</i>

00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:48.500
<i>The wind tickled my nose</i>

00:22:48.870 --> 00:22:51.540
<i>yamiyo ni magirete oeoeo</i>

00:22:48.870 --> 00:22:51.540
<i>Lost in the dark night, oeoeo</i>

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:54.300
<i>oeoeo oeoeo</i>

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:54.300
<i>Oeoeo oeoeo</i>

00:22:54.420 --> 00:22:56.760
<i>kimi no ushiro kara oeoeo</i>

00:22:54.420 --> 00:22:56.760
<i>From behind you, oeoeo</i>

00:22:56.880 --> 00:23:01.680
<i>oeoeo oeoe o o o</i>

00:22:56.880 --> 00:23:01.680
<i>Oeoeo oeoe o o o</i>

